as just another sorcerer just saying we  also discovered that Peters Aunt May may  be striking up a new romance with Tony  Stark's right-hand man  happy hogan how do we feel about this do  we ship this do kids still say that  almost definitely not we know for a fact  that Pete and his friends visit at least  two far-flung destinations Venice and  London and while he's on the road  Pete meets up with the founder of The  Avengers Nick Fury who apparently also  did not really die in the snap plus all  of his spy skills are clearly intact he  snuck into a room full of sleeping teens  fired a dart gun and had a full  conversation with Peter Parker without  waking anyone up the trailer indicates  that the villains in this new film will  be the elementals in the comics they're  a team of four whose powers allow them  to control natural forces there's  Hellfire who generates flames  hydron who controls water magnum who  manipulates earth and rocks and Zephyr  who controls air but it's entirely  possible that none of the elementals we  see in the film will actually be the  original comic book versions of these  characters many fans have speculated  that these villains are actually not the  original elementals at all but Moulton  man Hydra man and Sandman who all have  similar powers to the ones we see on  display Plus Hellfire already appeared  on TVs agents of shield bolstering this  theory check out this boat floating  behind Ned in Venice it's identified as  a SM - one - this could be a reference  to amazing spider-man issue - one -  which was the first to feature you  guessed it hydro man oh and check out  this shot of Nick Fury fighting the  movies rock monster who's the mysterious  woman fighting alongside him the most  probable candidate is Cobie Smulders aka  Maria hill she's credited as appearing  in far from home after also vanishing  alongside Nick in the snap but we think  this could also be Sharon Carter aka  agent 13 we last saw her aiding Captain  America and 